    <other_details id="References">Archetypes: openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-AGENT.generic_agent.v1, openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-PARTY_RELATIONSHIP.acting_on_behalf.v1, openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-PARTY_RELATIONSHIP.party_membership.v1, openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-PARTY_RELATIONSHIP.role_assignment.v1, openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.device.v1, openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.electronic_communication.v1. Aligned with the HL7 FHIR R4 (4.0.1) resource Device (https://hl7.org/fhir/R4/) and the published CKM cluster openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.device.v1.</other_details>
    <details>
      <language>
        <terminology_id>
          <value>ISO_639-1</value>
        </terminology_id>
        <code_string>en</code_string>
      </language>
      <purpose>A non-human actor, such as a software application, a device or a service, with its identifiers, type, maker, versions, status, electronic contacts and the parties it acts for.</purpose>
      <keywords>agent</keywords>
      <keywords>software</keywords>
      <keywords>application</keywords>
      <keywords>device</keywords>
      <keywords>service</keywords>
      <use>Use for an application, a device or a service that acts in its own name. An acting on behalf relationship names the organisation or person it acts for; a membership or a role assignment places it in a group, an organisation or a role.</use>
      <misuse>Not for a person who uses an application or a device.</misuse>
      <copyright>© openehr-reference-content contributors</copyright>
    </details>
  </description>
